@@ -171,6 +171,18 @@ Given an Exp 3883 K sweep completes, the artifact sets `accuracy_by_k`, `k_curve
 ## SCENARIO-EBT-3883-FALSIFICATION: Monotone K Gain Is Required For System-2 Support
 Given `accuracy_by_k` for K values `[1, 2, 4, 8, 16]`, Exp 3883 writes `k_curve_shape="MONOTONE_GAIN"` only when the curve is non-decreasing and K=16 accuracy is greater than K=1 accuracy; this yields a `complete: ebt_system2_SUPPORTED_acc_rises_with_k_best_k<k>_acc<a>` verdict. If the curve plateaus or degrades, Exp 3883 writes `complete: ebt_system2_BOUNDED_<shape>_no_usable_descent_signal_at_scale`.
 
+## REQ-EBT-3893: Thesis-A Fundamental Negative Independent Replication
+The system must provide `scripts/experiments/experiment_3893_ebt_fundamental_replication.py` to independently replicate the Exp 3882 `.359` FUNDAMENTAL result on two fresh seeds distinct from `{1, 2, 3}`. The workflow must check CUDA, the direct `thesis_a_part_b_scaled` scripts-path import, and reusable Exp 3882 measurement functions before live work. For each configured fresh seed, it must retrain the scaled EBT and matched AR control from scratch, reuse the Exp 3882 AR best-of-N, greedy energy-argmin, global cumulative-energy beam decode, and matched-FLOP accounting paths, and evaluate held-out examples sequentially. Seeds whose AR positive control is outside `[0.4, 0.95]` must be recorded but excluded from `n_valid_seeds`. The artifact must be written to `results/experiment_3893_ebt_fundamental_replication.json`, must use a terminal `complete:` or `blocked_` honest verdict, and must emit `replication_outcome`, `ebt_beam_accuracy_mean`, `ebt_argmin_accuracy_mean`, `ar_best_accuracy_mean`, `n_valid_seeds`, `matched_flops_ratio`, `seeds_used`, `n_heldout`, `retrained`, `preconditions_checked`, `model_specs`, `random_seed`, `random_seeds_used`, `reproducibility_checksum`, `duration_s`, and `inference_substrate` as bare JSON values.
+
+## SCENARIO-EBT-3893-REPLICATION-GATE: Fresh Valid Seeds Bank The Negative
+Given at least two valid fresh seeds, Exp 3893 writes `replication_outcome="REPLICATED"` and an honest verdict beginning `complete: ebt_fundamental_REPLICATED` only when mean EBT beam accuracy and mean greedy argmin accuracy are both below 20% of mean AR best-of-N accuracy. Given at least two valid seeds and mean EBT beam accuracy at least 50% of mean AR accuracy, it writes `replication_outcome="REFUTED"` and an honest verdict beginning `complete: ebt_fundamental_REFUTED`. Given fewer than two valid seeds, it writes `replication_outcome="INCONCLUSIVE"` and an honest verdict beginning `complete: ebt_fundamental_INCONCLUSIVE_only<n>_valid_seeds_ar_control_collapsed`.
+
+## SCENARIO-EBT-3893-SCHEMA: Replication Artifact Fields Are Bare Values
+Given completed or blocked Exp 3893 execution, the artifact sets `replication_outcome`, `ebt_beam_accuracy_mean`, `ebt_argmin_accuracy_mean`, `ar_best_accuracy_mean`, `n_valid_seeds`, `matched_flops_ratio`, `seeds_used`, `n_heldout`, `retrained`, `preconditions_checked`, `model_specs`, `random_seed`, `random_seeds_used`, `reproducibility_checksum`, `duration_s`, and `inference_substrate` as bare JSON bools, numbers, strings, arrays, or objects. None of those fields may be wrapped in a `{value, principle}` dictionary.
+
+## SCENARIO-EBT-3893-REUSE: Exp 3882 Measurement Path Is Reused
+Given Exp 3893 runs a fresh seed, it imports the Exp 3882 experiment module and delegates model training, AR best-of-N evaluation, greedy EBT argmin evaluation, global cumulative-energy EBT beam search, and matched-FLOP accounting to the Exp 3882 measurement functions. It may only override checkpoint selection to prevent reusing prior checkpoints for the fresh replication seeds.
+
 ## REQ-EBT-3731: Thesis-A EBT Bring-Up Capstone Aggregation
 The system must provide `scripts/experiment_3731_capstone_v341.py` to aggregate Exp 3724 through Exp 3730 from checked-in JSON artifacts only. The capstone must exclude any upstream artifact carrying `flagged_adversarial=true` from headline aggregation, cite every unflagged upstream artifact with imported fields and SHA256 hashes, preserve the paper-ready and frozen-headline invariants from Exp 3724, carry the kill-gate part-(a) verdict from Exp 3729, and write `results/experiment_3731_capstone_v341.json` with the required principle-annotated fields. The capstone must not claim that energy-as-generator works; `green_light_342=true` only means stable enough to run the matched-compute comparison, while `green_light_342=false` records Thesis-A as bounded at small scale.
 
